From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: playportdev <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:28:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 84/85] ntdll: a 4 GB floor constrains nothing on iOS

map_view lets a request escape the furniture ceiling, and raises its scan
floor to the guest window, only when its limit_low is at or below
address_space_start (ml119): such a floor is satisfied by any placement. On
iOS nothing is ever mapped below 4 GB (__PAGEZERO), so limit_4g is the same
case, but set_large_address_space puts address_space_start back to 0x10000
and the test missed it. Every x64 thread's CHPE emulator stack and a WoW64
thread's 64-bit stack (both limit_4g) therefore scanned bottom-up from 4 GB
through iOS's own 60 GB of low VA (700 to 1200 failed mach_vm_map calls per
thread), took the first hole there, and could not leave a full window
(Death's Door: DXMT's thread could not start). That boot grind is also what
latched ios_va_pressure on some launches and not others.

A limit_low at or below 0x100010000 is now treated as no floor.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-06-guest-va-exhaustion.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index 6176264..7f6e50f 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -11983,6 +11983,16 @@ static NTSTATUS map_view( struct file_view **view_ret, void *base, size_t size,
              * for the same call. (top_down is a hint, not a contract, and is
              * knowingly dropped on the relax path.) */
             ceiling_relaxable = (limit_low <= (ULONG_PTR)address_space_start);
+            /* Playport: on iOS nothing is ever mapped below 4 GB (__PAGEZERO), so
+             * a 4 GB floor (limit_4g: every x64 thread's CHPE emulator stack, a
+             * WoW64 thread's 64-bit stack) constrains nothing either. ml119's
+             * test missed it once set_large_address_space put address_space_start
+             * back to 0x10000: those requests got neither the floor raise nor the
+             * relax path, so each one scanned bottom-up from 4 GB through iOS's
+             * own 60 GB of low VA (700 to 1200 failed mach_vm_map calls per
+             * thread, the boot grind that latched ios_va_pressure on some
+             * launches and not others) and took the first hole there. */
+            if (limit_low <= 0x100010000ULL) ceiling_relaxable = 1;
         }
         size_t host_size = ROUND_SIZE( 0, size, host_page_mask );
         size_t unmap_size, view_size = host_size + align_mask + 1;
